    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0423" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.304M28/63.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-02">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi> 2, 1912</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Navy Department highly appreciates the honor contained in article four of the
                    President’s decree, relating to delivery by the Cuban Navy on board an American
                    war vessel of the remains taken from the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>. It
                    would, however, be practically more expedient for the American Navy to receive
                    the caskets at Caballería wharf and convey them to the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >North Carolina</hi>. You will urge upon the Cuban Government a modification
                    of the arrangements to this effect.</p>
                <p>The wreck of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> will probably not be removed
                    before March 14.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
